typos's list of misspellings, which is compiled into the typos binary,
includes entries taken from codespell's dictionary in 2023 and 2026 (commits
7523a865 "feat(dict): Pull in codespell items" and 54e13666 "feat(dict):
Extend from codespell's list" in crate-ci/typos). typos took a selection of
the entries and merged them into its own list, in its own format. The typos
repository keeps a copy of that dictionary in
crates/codespell-dict/assets/dictionary.txt.

codespell's dictionary (https://github.com/codespell-project/codespell) is a
derivative work of English Wikipedia. It is the codespell project's improved
version of the list of common misspellings that Wikipedia contributors
maintain at
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Lists_of_common_misspellings/For_machines

The codespell project releases it under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported License (CC BY-SA 3.0). The license text
is in the file CC-BY-SA-3.0 next to this one and at
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/.

typos also took entries from Wikipedia's list directly; see
../wikipedia/NOTICE.
